# NAVER Maps — Contact page (/contact) interactive office map
#
# When this variable is set, the /contact map square renders an interactive NAVER
# Dynamic Map centred on the Cinapi office with a marker. When it is absent, the
# square keeps the professional address fallback panel. The transition is automatic
# based on whether this variable exists.
#
# This is the PUBLIC browser Key ID for the NAVER Maps JavaScript API v3.
# In the NAVER Cloud Platform console:
#   - Enable "Web Dynamic Map"
#   - Register the service URLs (scheme + host only, no port and no path), e.g.:
#       http://localhost
#       https://cinapi.com
#
# Never use a Client Secret, Access Key, or Secret Key here — this value is inlined
# into the browser bundle.
#
# Put the real value in .env.local (git-ignored, never committed):
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_NAVER_MAP_NCP_KEY_ID=your_public_key_id
#
# Note: the "Open in NAVER Map" external link needs no key (plain NAVER search URL).
NEXT_PUBLIC_NAVER_MAP_NCP_KEY_ID=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Contact form delivery (/contact -> POST /api/contact)
#
# These are SERVER-ONLY. Never prefix them with NEXT_PUBLIC_ — that would inline
# the value into the browser bundle. Put real values in .env.local (git-ignored)
# for local testing, and in Vercel Project Settings -> Environment Variables for
# deployed environments.
#
# While any of the three are unset, /api/contact answers 503 "not_configured"
# and the form shows its error state. It never reports success.
#
# Provider: Resend (https://resend.com), called over its REST API.
#   1. Create an account and an API key           -> RESEND_API_KEY
#   2. Add and verify the sending domain (DNS records in the Resend dashboard).
#      Until a domain is verified, Resend only allows the onboarding sender and
#      only delivers to the account owner's own address — fine for a first test,
#      not for production.
#   3. CONTACT_FROM_EMAIL must be on the verified domain (e.g. no-reply@<domain>).
#      It stays the authenticated sender; the visitor's address is set as
#      reply_to instead, so replying reaches them without spoofing the domain.
#   4. CONTACT_TO_EMAIL is where inquiries arrive (the business address).
RESEND_API_KEY=
CONTACT_TO_EMAIL=
CONTACT_FROM_EMAIL=
